{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431312-necromancy-bloodlines-the-resurrected","id":1431312,"title":"Necromancy, Bloodlines the Resurrected","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-06T13:10:31-08:00","id":1431312,"title":"Necromancy, Bloodlines the Resurrected","content":"Hey! could someone help me with understanding the Necromancy rules in Bloodlines the Resurrected? <br /> <br /> Quicken Corpse (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) Target number of successes: 8 Material Focus: An intact humanoid corpse. The vampire touches a humanoid corpse and imbues it with necromantic power, animating it and creating a mindless but obedient follower. This creation is effectively a \u201cfree\u201d Retainer with a rating equal to the rite\u2019s Potency, with a \u201cfield\u201d mostly encompassing manual labor and basic forms of violence. Zombies do not suffer wound penalties and cannot heal damage naturally. Bashing, lethal and aggravated wounds are marked normally, but a zombie never suffers incapacitation \u2014 it just keeps going until its last Health box is lost to aggravated damage. When a zombie\u2019s rightmost Health box is marked with bashing or lethal damage, no roll is required to remain conscious. Casting this ritual on an existing zombie can heal damage equal to Potency. If the target corpse is already animated under Appendix I: Kindred Necromancy 24 another necromancer\u2019s control, a Clash of Wills takes place; if the vampire succeeds, he gains control of the corpse. This ritual ends after a lunar month, or whenever the zombie is destroyed from suffering aggravated damage in its rightmost health box.<br /> <br /> <br /> is Potency equal to success or the rank of the ritual? As the ritual requires 8 success if potency is 8 that would make them rank 8 retainers and have 16 dice to attack. Correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T13:37:15-08:00","id":1431316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1431312-necromancy-bloodlines-the-resurrected#post1431312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is Potency equal to success or the rank of the ritual? As the ritual requires 8 success if potency is 8 that would make them rank 8 retainers and have 16 dice to attack. Correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the sidebar on p152 of VtR2e core, Potency is one plus the number of successes above the target number; if you roll an exceptional success during the ritual, you can add your Discipline dots to Potency if the ritual succeeds.<br /> <br /> In other words, if you roll 8 successes you have a Potency 1 zombie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}